1
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:36,920
Flag presentation ceremony...

2
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:37,920
Begin!

3
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:39,520
Escort the flag!

4
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:42,240
Parade step, march!

5
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,720
Present the flag!

6
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:16,760
Receive the flag!

7
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:28,560
Salute!

8
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:28,280
Hello, Battalion Commander.

9
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:31,240
Please forgive me for leaving without saying goodbye.

10
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:35,400
All this time,

11
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,760
I have deeply loved this honorable profession,

12
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,160
giving it my all and fulfilling my duties.

13
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,080
For the military as a collective,

14
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,800
I hold a profound affection,

15
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:47,360
and I am genuinely proud of the title of a soldier.

16
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:48,480
But,

17
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,840
I can no longer keep up with the pace of military reform.

18
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:55,080
Leaving is the greatest contribution I can currently make

19
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,720
to the military.

20
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:58,920
As a veteran,

21
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,120
I promise,

22
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:01,800
If there is war,

23
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:03,440
I will answer the call.

24
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,560
One

25
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:48,040
Two

26
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,040
Three

27
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,160
Four

28
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:52,840
Battalion Commander.

29
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:55,120
Everyone's really fired up right now,

30
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,680
but space is limited.

31
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,600
We can only conduct single-branch training.

32
00:05:59,000 --> 00:05:59,800
Combined arms training

33
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:01,200
is falling short.

34
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:05,920
You want to apply for off-base training?

35
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:07,400
I'm just worried

36
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,080
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo won't agree.

37
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,360
What are you doing here?

38
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:37,120
Political Instructor, just sit down for a bit.

39
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:38,760
You've been pacing back and forth...

40
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:39,920
You've already walked eighteen laps.

41
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,200
You're making me so nervous.

42
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,440
I'll just take one more look.

43
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:45,800
Our Battalion Commander went to see Battalion Commander Jiang about the field training.

44
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,000
He's not going there to pick a fight.

45
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,120
What are you worried about?

46
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,440
I know that.

47
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,280
But those two...

48
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,760
are sworn enemies.

49
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,240
Whenever they meet...

50
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:57,040
they just go at each other's throats.

51
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:01,480
Staff Officer Liang,

52
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:04,400
do you think Jiang Shengqiang will agree?

53
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:13,760
No way.

54
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,880
Absolutely not.

55
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,200
Guo Zijian, let me tell you.

56
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,920
Don't think I don't know what you're trying to do.

57
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,000
Trying to use me as a pawn, right?

58
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:20,680
Not a chance.

59
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,080
How can you say that?

60
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:25,440
I bet you've had the same thought.

61
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:27,640
Even if I did, so what?

62
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:28,880
So what?

63
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,520
It can only remain a thought.

64
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:34,000
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo will never agree to it.

65
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,200
That's why we both need to

66
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,760
work together to convince him.

67
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:37,560
I'm not going.

68
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:39,600
I'm not going.

69
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:41,280
Nothing you say will work.

70
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:42,760
I'm telling you, I'm not going.

71
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:45,160
No means no. I'm not going!

72
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,200
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo,

73
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:06,360
since the Wind Rider Battalion

74
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:08,520
and the Hurricane Battalion were established,

75
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:10,440
we've been focusing on basic training.

76
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,440
But the foundation for new-type combined arms

77
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:14,920
was already laid solidly during the training camp.

78
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,080
And after two combined exercises,

79
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,520
the results have been quite good.

80
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,280
However, due to environmental constraints,

81
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:23,080
the live-equipment combined training for both battalions

82
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,560
hasn't been organized yet.

83
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:25,800
So I was thinking,

84
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,040
maybe we could take the troops out

85
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,480
and let them properly integrate.

86
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,400
The specialized basic training isn't over yet,

87
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:33,600
and you want to do combined training?

88
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:36,200
That goes against training principles.

89
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,240
Since the Wind Rider Battalion is part of the

90
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,960
new-type combat forces,

91
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,520
we should boldly experiment.

92
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:42,760
I was thinking,

93
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,520
could we skip

94
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,120
individual basic training

95
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,200
and directly proceed to

96
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:48,520
combined tactical training?

97
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,760
Then what about the new recruits joining us?

98
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,000
About that,

99
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,440
Battalion Commander Jiang and I have discussed it.

100
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:58,000
We could jointly set up an Advanced Recruit Training Camp.

101
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,280
What do you mean?

102
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,280
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo is asking you.

103
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,360
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo,

104
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:14,000
what Battalion Commander Guo means is,

105
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:14,960
the new recruits

106
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:17,320
will complete everything from basic to specialized training

107
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:20,480
entirely within this Advanced Recruit Training Camp.

108
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:23,480
Once they meet the combat-ready standard for companies,

109
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:24,680
they'll enter the combat units.

110
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:25,760
This way,

111
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:28,480
veteran battalions can freely focus on tactics,

112
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:29,400
while the recruit camp

113
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:30,800
can concentrate its efforts

114
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:31,680
on building the foundation.

115
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,000
This

116
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:34,520
kills two birds with one stone.

117
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,120
Following your proposed model,

118
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,600
in the future, from both battalions,

119
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,840
I would have to pull more key personnel

120
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:43,440
to train the new recruits.

121
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:46,200
That will affect the outcome of combined operations.

122
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:49,240
As for the integration you just mentioned,

123
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,560
I agree.

124
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:52,080
But we can't be reckless.

125
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,280
So I'll make a suggestion.

126
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,800
Let's have the Long-Range Rocket Unit

127
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:58,480
and the Air Assault Unit

128
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:02,160
invite their comrades to our base.

129
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:05,080
We'll sit down behind closed doors

130
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,640
and properly discuss tactics.

131
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,560
Wouldn't that be great?

132
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,240
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo,

133
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,880
it was stated at the Army's training mobilization

134
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,440
that war is a tough battle,

135
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:15,120
and training must be realistic.

136
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,200
Without troops or equipment,

137
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,360
how are we supposed to integrate?

138
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:19,920
First integrate your mindsets,

139
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:22,400
and integrate your concepts.

140
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:25,320
I think taking the troops out to the field,

141
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:27,760
into a realistic combat atmosphere, is better for training.

142
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:28,600
I think

143
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,400
we can do the same in the base.

144
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,240
As long as you put your heart into it,

145
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:33,800
you can create

146
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:35,280
a real combat atmosphere just the same.

147
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,360
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo,

148
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:39,200
our base's training ground is only so big.

149
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,040
Let alone realistic combat,

150
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,520
even for a simulation,

151
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:44,120
we can can't deploy this many men and equipment.

152
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:47,200
Anyway, following your plan is just messing around.

153
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:49,000
How can it be messing around?

154
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,760
We have a strict training organization plan.

155
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:52,680
Come on.

156
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,520
This is your training organization plan?

157
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:55,440
Here, let's take a look.

158
00:10:57,440 --> 00:11:00,080
Let's set aside this independent field training for now.

159
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,520
Let's talk about this mobilization.

160
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,720
You could have just said mobilization,

161
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:04,960
but you had to come up with some

162
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,320
Mission-Oriented Mobilization,

163
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,520
Discussion-Based Training,

164
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:13,520
and Multi-Dimensional Leapfrog Force Deployment.

165
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:14,640
Oh my God.

166
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:15,840
You really know how to make things up.

167
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:18,440
You make these concepts sound so flashy,

168
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:19,680
but how do you implement them?

169
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:23,560
Stop aiming too high.

170
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:27,320
Keep your feet on the ground, will you?

171
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:33,560
Have you investigated all the units?

172
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:35,440
Your battalion's...

173
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,160
Engineer Unit,

174
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,800
Technical Reconnaissance Unit,

175
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,440
the artillery brigade's Long-Range Rocket Battalion,

176
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:44,080
the assault brigade's Air Assault Unit.

177
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:48,640
Almost half of the basic training subjects

178
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:49,720
have not been completed.

179
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:51,200
And for those completed,

180
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,840
the excellence rate falls short.

181
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:56,880
How can you achieve your vision?

182
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,320
I actually did ask about that.

183
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:01,160
We can select the most outstanding soldiers from the units.

184
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:02,480
I've already said this just now.

185
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,320
We stay right in the camp.

186
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:05,440
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo,

187
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:08,400
with this kind of training in our camp,

188
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:10,120
dynamic becomes static,

189
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,520
live gear becomes simulation.

190
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,760
Not to mention the training effect is greatly compromised,

191
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:15,440
everyone just trains on their own.

192
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,480
This doesn't help build a sense of coordination.

193
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,240
Was Rome built in a day?

194
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:23,400
Let me ask you, was Rome built in a day?

195
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,920
A sense of coordination isn't built in a day either.

196
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:30,640
We must take it step by step, comrades.

197
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:32,200
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo is right.

198
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:36,160
Moving everyone out would cause too much of a stir.

199
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:40,160
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo,

200
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,560
how about this?

201
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:44,680
According to the scale of Friday's readiness mobilization,

202
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:46,560
let's organize a small-scale,

203
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:47,800
light-gear mobilization.

204
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,040
Light-gear won't do either.

205
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,480
Don't I know the two of you?

206
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:53,280
Especially Guo Zijian.

207
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,040
If you take the troops out of the camp,

208
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:56,360
he'd dare to pull anything.

209
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:58,720
How can I agree to this?

210
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,920
I promise,

211
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,960
not a single scratch on men or vehicles.

212
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,280
Moving vehicles always carries risks.

213
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:04,600
If something goes wrong,

214
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,560
it will affect the training schedule.

215
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:08,240
Then what about our...

216
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,040
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

217
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:10,640
Speak.

218
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:13,320
Our Wind Rider Battalion and Hurricane Battalion

219
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:16,120
are very different in both equipment and training models

220
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,760
from traditional army units.

221
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:21,920
We need to integrate many different specialties.

222
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,280
Purely from a tactical perspective,

223
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:25,600
our tactics inevitably require repeated coordination.

224
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:28,440
If we really follow what happens after recruits join their companies

225
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:30,200
and use the old method for training,

226
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:33,600
I'm afraid we won't complete the annual training tasks.

227
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:37,800
Staff Officer Zhou, what do you think?

228
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,640
What are you mumbling for?

229
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:44,520
Speak your mind.

230
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:44,960
Report.

231
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,360
The difficulties do exist.

232
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,240
To be honest,

233
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,000
your idea is very good.

234
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:00,880
I agree.

235
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:02,560
But you have to admit,

236
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:05,360
taking the troops' training habits of many years

237
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:06,880
and just breaking them

238
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:09,240
is very dangerous.

239
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,840
Pulling all the troops out of the camp

240
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:15,040
to organize combat-oriented training on the move...

241
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,120
Oh my God.

242
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,320
That's too big a step.

243
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:18,880
Actually, this training model,

244
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:20,200
we already used it in the training unit.

245
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,440
You know that too.

246
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:22,720
The training unit only had a few people.

247
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:26,640
I now have two whole battalions of troops and equipment.

248
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,840
The risk is too high.

249
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,120
Let's wait a bit longer.

250
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:32,440
Comrade Commander.

251
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:34,000
Please take another serious look

252
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,600
at our detailed plan.

253
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:37,240
It really is very thorough.

254
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,880
All the problems you are considering

255
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:39,960
are addressed right in here.

256
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:40,880
If something happens, who takes responsibility?

257
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,600
I will.

258
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:43,720
You make it sound so easy.

259
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:44,880
If something really happens,

260
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,200
can you afford the responsibility?

261
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,040
Jiang Shengqiang.

262
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:55,840
Sir!

263
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:57,520
After you go back,

264
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,400
you'd better seriously focus on

265
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,920
basic training.

266
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:01,760
Yes, sir!

267
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:10,560
I must have lost my mind

268
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:11,720
to make this trip with you.

269
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:13,560
How do you know unless you try?

270
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,680
You're usually so loud and cocky.

271
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,560
Why so timid in front of the leaders?

272
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:18,640
You dare not say a peep.

273
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,120
That's called respecting superiors.

274
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:22,120
Whatever you say.

275
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:23,880
I owe you one for this.

276
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:24,840
I'll buy you a meal some time.

277
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:25,640
No need.

278
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,360
I didn't do it for you.

279
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:29,360
I did it for my Hurricane Battalion.

280
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:30,640
I'm off.

281
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,400
Alright, stop looking.

282
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,600
The Combined Arms Battalion data you asked for,

283
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,880
I really don't have much here.

284
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,200
I'll have the Operations Section send you a set later.

285
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:55,920
Will that do?

286
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,120
Thank you, Commander.

287
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:02,880
How's your role as Chief Staff Officer?

288
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,320
To be honest,

289
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:09,320
it's much harder than being an Exercise Control Officer.

290
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:11,400
Hard?

291
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:12,880
How so?

292
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:15,840
Pushing the training plan forward

293
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:17,000
is difficult.

294
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,280
Difficult to push forward?

295
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:20,760
What's going on?

296
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,400
Commander,

297
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:24,560
if

298
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,560
I tell you directly,

299
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,360
would it count as bypassing the chain of command?

300
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:33,680
No wonder you were digging around.

301
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,120
You were just waiting to bring this up.

302
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:36,280
Staff Officer Liang,

303
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:38,520
you've picked up bad habits from Guo Zijian.

304
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:40,280
Beating around the bush.

305
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:43,400
Go ahead.

306
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,720
It won't count as bypassing.

307
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:45,680
Yes, sir.

308
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,480
It's quite simple, actually.

309
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,560
We believe the Value Cube,

310
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:52,400
its true charm and value,

311
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:54,200
lie in getting it spinning and moving.

312
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:57,200
So, we want to organize a

313
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,720
light-gear combat readiness mobilization,

314
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:01,720
and conduct combat-oriented field training on-site.

315
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,800
Just your battalion going out alone,

316
00:17:05,080 --> 00:17:07,560
plus the attached units?

317
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:11,280
That poses huge difficulties in management and training.

318
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:13,000
Sir,

319
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:16,880
we have already drafted a comprehensive field training plan.

320
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,560
You really came prepared.

321
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:24,040
Not bad.

322
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:29,640
But Deputy Brigade Commander Suo won't approve it.

323
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:37,800
It's not just Deputy Brigade Commander Suo who'd disagree,

324
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,280
even I can't approve it right away.

325
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,680
Your new team

326
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:44,600
has drive and innovation.

327
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:45,800
But sometimes,

328
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:47,760
you don't know your own limits.

329
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:50,440
You've caused quite a few messes in the past, right?

330
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:53,040
As the Chief Staff Officer of the Wind Rider Battalion,

331
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:54,360
the principles you must uphold

332
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:55,640
cannot be compromised.

333
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:56,680
Sir,

334
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,320
I believe there are no issues with our principles.

335
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:00,880
Alright.

336
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,760
You're all one family now.

337
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:06,040
How about this:

338
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:07,480
I'll go take a look at the troops first.

339
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:08,320
Let's go.

340
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:10,400
Yes, sir.

341
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,920
How is everyone's training going?

342
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:25,240
Reporting, Brigade Commander.

343
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:27,880
Currently, the Firepower Company is only focusing on basic training.

344
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:28,640
We aren't using the equipment.

345
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:29,720
So,

346
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,080
we're making do.

347
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:33,400
Making do?

348
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:49,880
It's time.

349
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,520
I know our training time is up.

350
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:54,760
But your training time hasn't even started yet, has it?

351
00:18:54,880 --> 00:18:55,640
Ten minutes.

352
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,720
Just ten minutes.

353
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:58,040
We'll definitely clear out, okay?

354
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,920
You're pulling this trick again, huh?

355
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:00,720
No way.

356
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:02,520
Let them practice a bit more.

357
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:03,280
Hurry up.

358
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:04,040
You two over there.

359
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:11,240
Sir.

360
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:11,960
Sir.

361
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:13,160
What's going on here?

362
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,520
Trying to start a fight?

363
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:15,360
We're not fighting.

364
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:16,560
Right, no fighting.

365
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:18,240
As long as we don't do tactical integration,

366
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,360
we can make do with anything.

367
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:20,120
Make do?

368
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,040
You can't just make do in training.

369
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:23,000
Yes, sir.

370
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,200
Alright.

371
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:26,280
Go back and train hard.

372
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:26,760
Yes, sir.

373
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:28,720
Staff Officer Liang.

374
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:29,400
Yes, sir.

375
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,240
Tell me about

376
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,040
the training status of your new-type specialized units.

377
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,400
The new-type combined forces,

378
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:38,000
although close in scale to two branch companies,

379
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:39,320
involve complex specialties

380
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,320
and detailed classifications.

381
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:41,720
They are typical niche specialties,

382
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:42,960
or even highly refined ones.

383
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,120
If

384
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:46,400
we just go with the flow of the brigade,

385
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,640
or even join the group army's mass integration,

386
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:50,120
how will the training turn out?

387
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:50,840
To be honest,

388
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,480
I have no idea either.

389
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,680
Why do I feel like after all this talk,

390
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,080
it's all about making do,

391
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,120
settling,

392
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:02,400
and having no idea?

393
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:06,840
Commander.

394
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:10,280
Commander.

395
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,440
What our situation is like,

396
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:13,560
you've seen it yourself.

397
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:15,400
Right now, Wind Rider Battalion

398
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:17,680
has a different structure from the original Combined Arms Battalion.

399
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:19,240
It's like a hodgepodge.

400
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:20,680
Everyone is training together.

401
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:22,200
If we don't settle,

402
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:23,560
what else can we do?

403
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:26,280
Isn't it the same for Hurricane Battalion?

404
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:27,720
Why haven't I heard them

405
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:29,200
complaining or making snide remarks?

406
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:31,240
Not complaining doesn't mean the problem doesn't exist.

407
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:32,440
How about

408
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,320
you go check out Hurricane Battalion too?

409
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:35,480
You kid,

410
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:37,120
you're trying to force my hand.

411
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:37,760
I wouldn't dare.

412
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:39,520
Commander.

413
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:40,440
You're here.

414
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:41,920
Why didn't you give us a heads-up?

415
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:43,720
So we could prepare properly.

416
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,120
Cut the act, all of you.

417
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,840
Did you think this little act of yours

418
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:49,720
would go unnoticed?

419
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:55,120
Regarding this field training matter,

420
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:56,960
the brigade will look into it further.

421
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:57,920
Alright.

422
00:20:58,720 --> 00:20:59,760
What are you so happy about?

423
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,200
I haven't agreed yet.

424
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:04,120
You're a brilliant leader, Commander.

425
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:05,840
I'm sure you'll give us a satisfactory answer.

426
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,120
Stop flattering me.

427
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:07,920
Let's go.

428
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:16,840
Come in.

429
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:19,040
Old Liu.

430
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,360
What's up?

431
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:24,360
I need to discuss something with you.

432
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,640
Guo Zijian had Liang Hong

433
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:29,600
invite Commander Xu to inspect the Wind Rider Battalion.

434
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:31,440
He was complaining non-stop.

435
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:32,960
Reading between the lines,

436
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,760
he just wants to go for off-base training.

437
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:36,880
They went straight to Commander Xu?

438
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:37,760
Exactly!

439
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,240
What kind of behavior is that?

440
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:40,800
Bypassing the chain of command!

441
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:42,560
Where does that leave Deputy Brigade Commander Suo?

442
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:44,720
It's obvious

443
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:46,480
they're using the commander to pressure us.

444
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:48,560
Old Liu,

445
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:51,040
you might be overthinking this.

446
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:53,000
Training inside the base here

447
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,000
is indeed a bit too cramped.

448
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,760
What do you mean cramped?

449
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,120
What's stopping them from dealing with it?

450
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:58,640
Taking so many people out for off-base training,

451
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,560
how will they manage it?

452
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:02,160
If some safety accident happens,

453
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:03,080
what are they going to do?

454
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:05,520
I find that you people who aren't in management

455
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:06,880
really don't worry about these things.

456
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,320
Besides,

457
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:11,160
lately,

458
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:13,320
you've been taking their side.

459
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:16,000
What do you mean taking their side?

460
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:17,720
Old Liu,

461
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:20,440
isn't our 396th Brigade all one family?

462
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,160
I get it.

463
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,160
You don't like Guo Zijian,

464
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:25,400
right?

465
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:28,320
I don't like him either, I admit.

466
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:31,640
But work is work, and personal is personal.

467
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,160
Fair competition is fine,

468
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,080
but infighting

469
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,320
is unnecessary.

470
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:38,760
Who's infighting?

471
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:40,240
Old Liu.

472
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:42,440
Fine, let's drop it.

473
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:44,120
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo's support...

474
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:46,520
I will definitely use my actions

475
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:48,080
and achievements to repay it.

476
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:49,600
And I believe

477
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:51,320
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo

478
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:53,920
is also a broad-minded person,

479
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:54,840
right?

480
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:57,360
Fine, fine, fine.

481
00:22:57,800 --> 00:22:59,160
You're all broad-minded.

482
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,640
I'm still going to report to Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

483
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:03,360
Wait, Old Liu.

484
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:04,680
Old Liu!

485
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:05,480
Get some sleep.

486
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:19,160
All officers of the Wind Rider Battalion are mostly in place.

487
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:21,040
The only issue is the First Company's acting commander.

488
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:22,720
Staff Officer Huang is going back soon.

489
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:24,920
At a time like this,

490
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:28,400
who's best suited to be the First Company commander?

491
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:31,680
What are your thoughts?

492
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:33,920
I've considered so many people,

493
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:35,880
and I personally think

494
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:38,120
he is the most suitable one.

495
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:41,560
We're on the same page.

496
00:23:42,080 --> 00:23:43,160
I personally suggest

497
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:45,440
having an officer from the First Battalion

498
00:23:45,600 --> 00:23:47,760
take over as the First Company commander.

499
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:49,760
That way, they'll work better together.

500
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:52,880
But for this matter,

501
00:23:54,880 --> 00:23:56,240
you still need to test the waters.

502
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:58,640
Everyone in our company disagrees.

503
00:23:58,840 --> 00:23:59,880
Zeng Muhan

504
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:01,800
has the educational background

505
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:03,160
and the skills.

506
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:04,120
He is highly proficient

507
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:05,840
and cautious.

508
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:08,880
Him taking over from Li Songwei would be seamless.

509
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:10,080
Why are you so against it?

510
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:12,240
What skills does he have?

511
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,200
Back then,

512
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:15,440
not only did he misjudge the Blue Force command post,

513
00:24:15,520 --> 00:24:17,200
but during the second reconnaissance,

514
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:18,440
he was even taken prisoner.

515
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,480
If he hadn't been so useless,

516
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:22,160
nothing would've happened to Squad Leader Wu.

517
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:24,440
Political Instructor,

518
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:26,480
the position of our company commander

519
00:24:27,440 --> 00:24:29,200
only opened up because Commander Li

520
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:30,040
made a huge sacrifice.

521
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:31,720
If you're going to pick someone,

522
00:24:32,760 --> 00:24:33,880
you need to pick the best.

523
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:35,960
Is that really what they said?

524
00:24:37,840 --> 00:24:40,240
Li Songwei just left the First Company.

525
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:42,360
It's emotionally hard for the soldiers to accept,

526
00:24:42,360 --> 00:24:43,440
which is understandable.

527
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:45,360
But at a time like this,

528
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:47,920
sending Zeng Muhan over there

529
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:49,280
is actually

530
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:51,080
going to make it hard for him to do his job.

531
00:24:57,480 --> 00:24:59,160
The resumes you showed me last time...

532
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:02,320
There was a guy named Wang Qilin.

533
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:03,880
How is he?

534
00:25:04,120 --> 00:25:05,200
This Wang Qilin...

535
00:25:05,280 --> 00:25:07,680
He has a master's in military command.

536
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:10,000
He was a straight-A student in school.

537
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:13,160
He's actually a promising talent

538
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:15,280
highly valued by the brigade's training section.

539
00:25:15,800 --> 00:25:16,760
The brigade leaders

540
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:17,760
have always intended

541
00:25:17,760 --> 00:25:20,040
for him to gain more experience at the grassroots level.

542
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:25,360
Then let him go to the First Company

543
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,480
to fill in for a while.

544
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:28,880
We'll figure out the rest later.

545
00:25:33,040 --> 00:25:34,280
I figured

546
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,200
you'd be looking for me these next few days.

547
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:39,360
You can't let Guo Zijian and the others mess around.

548
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:41,880
Of course,

549
00:25:42,160 --> 00:25:43,200
we can't let them mess around.

550
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:44,520
It's true that

551
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:45,800
in terms of training,

552
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:48,040
they have a certain degree of autonomy.

553
00:25:48,320 --> 00:25:49,280
But whatever they do,

554
00:25:49,520 --> 00:25:50,720
they must follow the rules, right?

555
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,400
For my Combined Arms Battalion,

556
00:25:54,760 --> 00:25:57,000
hundreds of men and over a hundred vehicles...

557
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:59,040
They just mobilized out of nowhere.

558
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:00,600
Once they're out in the field,

559
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:01,400
how will they be managed?

560
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:02,640
How will they be trained?

561
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:03,640
Exactly!

562
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:05,760
Some units don't even belong to us.

563
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:06,960
How are we supposed to manage them?

564
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:07,880
It's so difficult!

565
00:26:11,120 --> 00:26:12,840
Isn't this a massive joke?

566
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:13,880
If you ask me,

567
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:15,600
just stay in the barracks

568
00:26:15,760 --> 00:26:16,880
and behave.

569
00:26:17,440 --> 00:26:19,000
Why cause all this trouble?

570
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:20,480
Right.

571
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,600
You and I are on the same page.

572
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:24,960
So yesterday, I took a walk around the barracks.

573
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:27,320
But I noticed that

574
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:28,440
a few companies

575
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:30,040
were fighting over training grounds

576
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:31,320
and almost came to blows.

577
00:26:31,360 --> 00:26:32,280
What's going on here?

578
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:35,120
This has to be resolved!

579
00:26:36,520 --> 00:26:37,600
So I was thinking,

580
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:40,200
why not just have Hurricane Battalion and Wind Rider Battalion

581
00:26:40,320 --> 00:26:41,480
mobilize completely?

582
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:43,600
For one, it solves the training ground issue.

583
00:26:43,720 --> 00:26:44,120
Secondly,

584
00:26:44,320 --> 00:26:46,440
it speeds up their training exploration process.

585
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:47,720
What do you think?

586
00:26:51,120 --> 00:26:52,840
Actually, the situation in the battalions...

587
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:54,600
I'm very clear about it.

588
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:56,960
If we mobilize the troops,

589
00:26:57,600 --> 00:26:58,560
it certainly

590
00:26:58,640 --> 00:26:59,880
would be a viable option.

591
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:01,320
Even so,

592
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:03,080
we must prepare a contingency plan in advance.

593
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:05,200
We need a solid training plan.

594
00:27:05,680 --> 00:27:06,920
We can't just ignore it.

595
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:08,680
Of course we can't ignore it.

596
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:11,680
So you and the Chief of Staff must keep a close eye on it.

597
00:27:15,120 --> 00:27:16,520
But the problem is,

598
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,720
apart from Guo Zijian,

599
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:19,880
I noticed that

600
00:27:20,160 --> 00:27:21,520
Jiang Shengqiang

601
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:23,400
seems to have lost his mind recently, too.

602
00:27:23,960 --> 00:27:24,800
I'm worried that

603
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:26,360
putting these two guys together

604
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:28,160
will cause trouble.

605
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:29,520
Therefore,

606
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:31,240
we must send a

607
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:32,200
senior

608
00:27:32,320 --> 00:27:33,600
and experienced brigade leader

609
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:34,560
to supervise the training.

610
00:27:37,680 --> 00:27:38,600
Thinking about this...

611
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:43,160
Old Suo,

612
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:44,160
look,

613
00:27:46,280 --> 00:27:49,200
you were personally chosen by the group army leaders.

614
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:51,000
Only if you step in personally

615
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:52,000
can you keep those two in line.

616
00:27:53,280 --> 00:27:54,080
I say, Commander,

617
00:27:54,600 --> 00:27:55,800
don't flatter me.

618
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:58,080
Jiang Shengqiang

619
00:27:59,080 --> 00:27:59,800
is not a problem.

620
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,440
But this Guo Zijian...

621
00:28:04,280 --> 00:28:05,480
I'm not so sure about him.

622
00:28:05,640 --> 00:28:06,400
Don't worry.

623
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:09,760
The brigade will give you carte blanche first.

624
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:15,200
Why do I feel

625
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:16,600
like you have some ulterior motives?

626
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:18,000
Do you want some water?

627
00:28:18,600 --> 00:28:19,240
I'll have some.

628
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:27,280
Give it a try.

629
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:34,280
Jiang Shengqiang.

630
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:35,920
Shouldn't you be thanking me?

631
00:28:35,920 --> 00:28:37,560
It's not like you did it for our Hurricane Battalion.

632
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:38,400
Either way,

633
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:39,920
I did the work, and you're reaping the rewards.

634
00:28:40,360 --> 00:28:41,680
Now that we're doing mobilization training,

635
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:42,800
want to compete?

636
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:45,040
You're on. Think I'm scared of you?

637
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:45,600
Bring it on!

638
00:28:57,040 --> 00:28:57,760
Xu Zhiqiang!

639
00:28:57,760 --> 00:28:58,200
Here!

640
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,320
Are there any problems?

641
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:06,360
No problems.

642
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:08,560
The gauges on this vehicle are a bit off.

643
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:09,760
I'm resetting them to zero.

644
00:29:11,120 --> 00:29:13,240
What do you think of your acting company commander?

645
00:29:14,600 --> 00:29:15,400
He's quite knowledgeable.

646
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:16,320
That's good.

647
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:18,080
You all should get some rest too.

648
00:29:18,160 --> 00:29:19,160
Recharge your energy.

649
00:29:19,280 --> 00:29:19,800
Understood?

650
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:20,520
Yes, sir!

651
00:29:23,560 --> 00:29:24,360
Staff Officer Liang.

652
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:24,960
Yes, sir.

653
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,360
Tomorrow's entire operation

654
00:29:26,440 --> 00:29:27,640
will go exactly as you designed.

655
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:28,400
Are you good with that?

656
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:29,040
No problems.

657
00:29:29,880 --> 00:29:31,120
Good attitude.

658
00:29:31,120 --> 00:29:32,440
You're quite calm and collected.

659
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:34,400
But during the training process,

660
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:36,120
all kinds of unexpected situations will occur.

661
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:37,000
Can you handle them?

662
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:38,560
I've already analyzed

663
00:29:38,560 --> 00:29:39,800
all the data,

664
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:41,960
and every potential situation

665
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:42,920
has been anticipated.

666
00:29:44,360 --> 00:29:45,840
But no matter how good the theory is,

667
00:29:45,920 --> 00:29:47,000
if you don't test it in the field,

668
00:29:47,360 --> 00:29:48,800
no one knows how it truly holds up.

669
00:29:49,080 --> 00:29:50,680
If you want to be a good chief staff officer,

670
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:52,640
just having theory won't cut it.

671
00:29:52,640 --> 00:29:54,800
Especially your future information platform,

672
00:29:54,800 --> 00:29:56,600
where and how to build it

673
00:29:56,760 --> 00:29:58,320
will all require battlefield trials first.

674
00:29:58,320 --> 00:29:59,240
Rest assured.

675
00:29:59,240 --> 00:30:00,840
I'm not an armchair strategist.

676
00:30:01,320 --> 00:30:03,280
Battalion Commander, your usual style

677
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:05,040
is to trust those you use and not use those you doubt.

678
00:30:05,040 --> 00:30:06,840
Why is it that when it comes to Staff Officer Liang,

679
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:08,120
you always throw cold water on her?

680
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:09,920
I'm just worried she'll get

681
00:30:09,920 --> 00:30:11,920
carried away and end up failing.

682
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:14,080
That kind of thing will absolutely never happen to me.

683
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:14,720
Good.

684
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:17,240
Then here's to a successful first battle.

685
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:18,120
Success!

686
00:30:18,240 --> 00:30:18,840
Success!

687
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:25,320
Emergency assembly!

688
00:31:06,080 --> 00:31:07,120
Attention, all companies.

689
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:08,720
Per brigade command's orders,

690
00:31:08,880 --> 00:31:10,120
our unit, fully manned and equipped,

691
00:31:10,120 --> 00:31:11,720
will rapidly deploy to the Wuyin Mountain area.

692
00:31:11,720 --> 00:31:13,360
The route has been sent to all command terminals.

693
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:14,240
Please check and confirm.

694
00:31:14,360 --> 00:31:15,680
Yes, copy that.

695
00:31:29,120 --> 00:31:30,520
Since it's raining,

696
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:33,240
do you think our mobilization will be canceled?

697
00:31:34,520 --> 00:31:35,640
Keep dreaming.

698
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:49,160
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo

699
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:50,720
The rain is getting heavier.

700
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:52,720
Should we delay the departure?

701
00:31:53,320 --> 00:31:55,360
It's much worse than the forecast predicted.

702
00:31:55,760 --> 00:31:58,360
It'd be fine with the brigade's Combined Arms Battalion.

703
00:31:58,360 --> 00:31:59,760
After all, Guo Zijian has

704
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:01,880
experience building bridges in valleys.

705
00:32:02,160 --> 00:32:03,920
But this time is completely different.

706
00:32:04,280 --> 00:32:05,800
Guo Zijian has forcefully

707
00:32:05,880 --> 00:32:06,960
turned this deployment into

708
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:10,080
a fully armed combat drill for the Wind Rider Battalion.

709
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:13,320
He even involved the Long-Range Rocket and Air Assault Units.

710
00:32:13,920 --> 00:32:15,120
What if...

711
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:18,920
Have the orders been relayed?

712
00:32:19,080 --> 00:32:19,640
Yes, they have.

713
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:20,400
What time is the departure?

714
00:32:20,400 --> 00:32:21,000
Eight o'clock.

715
00:32:22,720 --> 00:32:23,720
Three minutes left.

716
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:27,560
Make the call. Delay the departure.

717
00:32:27,720 --> 00:32:28,200
Yes, sir.

718
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:32,720
Wind Rider Battalion, Hurricane Battalion.

719
00:32:32,880 --> 00:32:34,680
Departure is delayed. Time TBD.

720
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:35,600
Please acknowledge.

721
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:37,520
Hurricane Battalion copies.

722
00:32:37,880 --> 00:32:38,960
Delaying departure.

723
00:32:40,200 --> 00:32:41,880
Wind Rider Battalion, Wind Rider Battalion.

724
00:32:41,880 --> 00:32:42,960
Please acknowledge.

725
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:45,200
Wind Rider Battalion, Wind Rider Battalion.

726
00:32:46,520 --> 00:32:47,880
Guo Zijian, Guo Zijian.

727
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:54,200
This is an order.

728
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:00,120
Catch up to the convoy.

729
00:33:00,280 --> 00:33:00,800
Move out.

730
00:33:01,280 --> 00:33:01,720
Move out.

731
00:33:19,480 --> 00:33:20,320
Dongfang.

732
00:33:21,200 --> 00:33:23,360
Even if it rains knives today,

733
00:33:23,520 --> 00:33:24,640
it won't stop

734
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:27,520
our battalion's strong steps toward a powerful military.

735
00:33:27,800 --> 00:33:28,680
Squad Leader.

736
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:31,080
Don't you mean 'resounding steps'?

737
00:33:32,840 --> 00:33:34,640
Am I the Squad Leader, or are you?

738
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:35,840
You're the Squad Leader.

739
00:33:36,080 --> 00:33:37,680
Then do I call the shots, or do you?

740
00:33:38,640 --> 00:33:39,600
You call the shots.

741
00:33:40,160 --> 00:33:41,320
Strong steps!

742
00:33:55,440 --> 00:33:57,800
Hurricane Battalion's scout platoon is like a swarm of flies.

743
00:33:58,280 --> 00:33:59,480
With all those cameras and lenses.

744
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:01,560
We can just ignore them, right?

745
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:02,960
Let's just focus on our own tasks.

746
00:34:02,960 --> 00:34:04,120
Easy for you to say.

747
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,040
If they figure us out completely,

748
00:34:06,040 --> 00:34:06,920
will you be happy then?

749
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:08,280
Keep your eyes peeled.

750
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:23,040
Go up front and keep an eye on the heavy equipment.

751
00:34:23,040 --> 00:34:24,120
Make sure nothing goes wrong.

752
00:34:24,120 --> 00:34:24,600
Yes, sir!

753
00:34:24,640 --> 00:34:25,560
Mount up!

754
00:34:39,440 --> 00:34:41,120
They're driving way too fast.

755
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:43,640
They have zero regard for safety.

756
00:34:45,600 --> 00:34:46,680
Did you find the command vehicle?

757
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:47,440
Don't bother.

758
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,280
He's definitely doing it on purpose.

759
00:34:49,640 --> 00:34:50,560
We've gone back and forth,

760
00:34:50,560 --> 00:34:52,280
looked two or three times and still can't find it.

761
00:34:52,600 --> 00:34:53,960
He must have slipped away long ago.

762
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:58,480
Long-Range Rocket Unit, report your position.

763
00:34:59,200 --> 00:34:59,720
Reporting.

764
00:34:59,960 --> 00:35:02,440
Long-Range Rocket Unit has reached Yuancun intersection.

765
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:05,240
According to the plan you designed,

766
00:35:05,720 --> 00:35:06,800
we should exit the highway

767
00:35:06,880 --> 00:35:07,880
and enter the field camp area.

768
00:35:07,880 --> 00:35:09,240
Do we continue as planned?

769
00:35:11,520 --> 00:35:12,680
No time to think.

770
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:16,920
Proceed.

771
00:35:19,520 --> 00:35:20,400
I order your unit

772
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:22,000
to change the march route immediately.

773
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:23,360
Exit the highway at Yuancun intersection,

774
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:24,680
take Country Road 4,

775
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:25,840
and enter the field camp area.

776
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:27,080
Country Road 4?

777
00:35:27,920 --> 00:35:28,720
Battalion Commander Guo,

778
00:35:29,240 --> 00:35:31,040
if we enter via Country Road 4,

779
00:35:31,320 --> 00:35:32,760
we'll have to cross Majia River.

780
00:35:33,200 --> 00:35:34,360
Our unit's equipment

781
00:35:34,360 --> 00:35:35,400
is oversized and overweight,

782
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:36,280
so we can't pass.

783
00:35:36,320 --> 00:35:38,160
The engineer unit will advance immediately to build a bridge.

784
00:35:38,160 --> 00:35:39,280
Your unit will follow them.

785
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:40,480
Battalion Commander Guo,

786
00:35:41,080 --> 00:35:42,240
a battalion-level engineer unit

787
00:35:42,480 --> 00:35:43,040
probably

788
00:35:43,920 --> 00:35:46,160
can't build heavy bridge structures.

789
00:35:46,200 --> 00:35:47,840
I'm not discussing this with you.

790
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:48,880
Execute the order.

791
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:49,800
Yes, sir.

792
00:35:54,680 --> 00:35:56,800
The one in direct charge holds the real power.

793
00:35:57,360 --> 00:35:58,600
Attention, Long-Range Rocket Unit.

794
00:35:58,960 --> 00:36:00,680
Exit the highway at Yuancun intersection.

795
00:36:01,240 --> 00:36:03,280
Take Country Road 4 via Majia River,

796
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:04,680
and head to the training site.

797
00:36:20,720 --> 00:36:21,920
Don't get stuck!

798
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:31,160
Move, move, move!

799
00:36:31,160 --> 00:36:31,760
Hurry up, hurry up!

800
00:36:38,120 --> 00:36:39,560
This Guo Zijian...

801
00:36:41,160 --> 00:36:42,600
...is such a pain.

802
00:36:48,240 --> 00:36:49,080
Platoon Leader Song!

803
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:50,560
Platoon Leader Song!

804
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:52,360
Salute!

805
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:55,040
Why aren't you crossing the bridge?

806
00:36:55,240 --> 00:36:55,920
Battalion Commander Guo.

807
00:36:56,160 --> 00:36:58,360
The bridge set up by the engineer unit doesn't meet standards.

808
00:36:58,360 --> 00:36:59,680
We can't risk crossing it.

809
00:36:59,680 --> 00:37:00,720
The bridge looks perfectly fine.

810
00:37:00,720 --> 00:37:01,680
Why can't we cross it?

811
00:37:01,840 --> 00:37:03,040
The bridge can't support the weight.

812
00:37:03,120 --> 00:37:03,720
Moreover,

813
00:37:03,880 --> 00:37:05,760
its construction doesn't meet combat standards.

814
00:37:05,920 --> 00:37:06,600
Is that true?

815
00:37:06,760 --> 00:37:07,160
Yes.

816
00:37:07,280 --> 00:37:09,120
Why wasn't it built to combat standards?

817
00:37:09,120 --> 00:37:09,680
Battalion Commander,

818
00:37:09,760 --> 00:37:10,720
setting up this kind of bridge...

819
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:12,760
...isn't like doing it on the mountain ridges of Wasp Waist Valley.

820
00:37:12,920 --> 00:37:13,760
As you can see,

821
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:15,600
there's mud everywhere.   We can't get any leverage.

822
00:37:15,600 --> 00:37:16,760
Of course,   the main reason is...

823
00:37:16,760 --> 00:37:17,640
Don't give me excuses!

824
00:37:17,640 --> 00:37:18,080
But...

825
00:37:18,080 --> 00:37:19,960
I must get all the equipment across this bridge today.

826
00:37:20,080 --> 00:37:20,520
But...

827
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:21,360
But what?

828
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:23,200
If we can't cross,   I'll discipline you.

829
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:23,760
Yes, sir!

830
00:37:35,280 --> 00:37:36,160
How did this happen?

831
00:37:36,440 --> 00:37:37,720
You're asking me? Who should I ask?

832
00:37:39,280 --> 00:37:40,920
You saw this coming, didn't you?

833
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:41,560
That's right.

834
00:37:41,840 --> 00:37:42,920
I saw it coming.

835
00:37:43,040 --> 00:37:44,640
But as the Chief Staff Officer,

836
00:37:44,680 --> 00:37:47,240
and the chief architect of this march plan,

837
00:37:47,240 --> 00:37:48,440
why didn't you see it?

838
00:37:48,960 --> 00:37:49,440
And another thing.

839
00:37:50,200 --> 00:37:52,120
Troops on the march can take side roads,

840
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:54,760
but you didn't investigate the off-road conditions at all.

841
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:55,840
Yet you dared to get off the highway.

842
00:37:56,080 --> 00:37:57,720
Then since you'd already seen

843
00:37:57,720 --> 00:37:58,480
the problems in the march plan,

844
00:37:58,480 --> 00:37:59,480
why didn't you say something earlier?

845
00:37:59,480 --> 00:38:00,640
Why should I have spoken up earlier?

846
00:38:00,640 --> 00:38:01,920
Why should I have warned you?

847
00:38:02,240 --> 00:38:03,520
You are the Chief Staff Officer.

848
00:38:03,520 --> 00:38:04,520
Not the other way around.

849
00:38:04,600 --> 00:38:06,240
You should be the one doing the homework,

850
00:38:06,240 --> 00:38:07,680
not me, the Commander.

851
00:38:15,840 --> 00:38:17,960
Do you think being a Commander is that simple?

852
00:38:18,080 --> 00:38:19,040
You give an order,

853
00:38:19,040 --> 00:38:20,840
and all the soldiers must charge into battle.

854
00:38:21,120 --> 00:38:22,120
Let me tell you,

855
00:38:22,200 --> 00:38:23,600
even for a Squad Leader,

856
00:38:23,680 --> 00:38:25,120
every single order he gives

857
00:38:25,120 --> 00:38:26,720
must be grounded in reality.

858
00:38:27,440 --> 00:38:29,120
Let alone the Chief Staff Officer.

859
00:38:29,520 --> 00:38:31,040
Every single order you give

860
00:38:31,040 --> 00:38:33,120
could affect the Commander's judgment,

861
00:38:33,240 --> 00:38:33,840
or even

862
00:38:34,080 --> 00:38:35,760
dictate the course of the battle.

863
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:38,000
Does my plan still have any value?

864
00:38:38,120 --> 00:38:38,840
Of course it does.

865
00:38:39,760 --> 00:38:40,880
Why are you doubting yourself?

866
00:38:41,040 --> 00:38:41,400
Let's go.

867
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:07,000
Battalion Commander,

868
00:39:07,640 --> 00:39:09,720
do you think Guo Zijian has a masochistic streak?

869
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,600
Instead of taking the perfectly good highway,

870
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:13,200
he insists on taking these country roads.

871
00:39:13,520 --> 00:39:14,240
Now look,

872
00:39:14,680 --> 00:39:15,560
it's a complete mess.

873
00:39:16,960 --> 00:39:18,200
Let them stew in it.

874
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:20,000
It's our turn now.

875
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:21,760
Order all companies

876
00:39:22,440 --> 00:39:24,600
to prepare for mobilization as planned.

877
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:25,680
Yes, sir.

878
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:33,560
To be honest, I just joined the company,

879
00:39:34,200 --> 00:39:35,480
so I really shouldn't complain.

880
00:39:36,760 --> 00:39:38,920
But this promising start turning into a crushing blow

881
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:41,960
only proves one thing.

882
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:45,440
The battalion's command plan is definitely flawed.

883
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:47,000
Staff Officer Liang

884
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:48,880
hasn't worked on the frontline before, after all.

885
00:39:49,520 --> 00:39:50,520
She lacks experience.

886
00:39:53,040 --> 00:39:54,360
That's no excuse.

887
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:55,600
You know what?

888
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:57,520
I spent very little time in frontline companies.

889
00:39:57,920 --> 00:39:59,720
Half a year max as a platoon leader after graduation.

890
00:40:00,120 --> 00:40:00,880
After that,

891
00:40:01,680 --> 00:40:03,880
I got into the military command graduate program.

892
00:40:04,280 --> 00:40:05,360
To tell you the truth,

893
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:08,760
I only did it for the sake of my future,

894
00:40:09,720 --> 00:40:12,400
to add grass-roots leadership experience to my record.

895
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:13,840
Otherwise,

896
00:40:15,080 --> 00:40:16,400
why would I leave the Operations and Training Section?

897
00:40:24,720 --> 00:40:25,600
Guo Zijian.

898
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:27,680
Do you have any sense of organization or discipline?

899
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:29,680
Who gave you the nerve

900
00:40:29,840 --> 00:40:31,720
to disobey orders and act on your own?

901
00:40:31,800 --> 00:40:32,600
What orders?

902
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:34,200
Don't play dumb.

903
00:40:34,600 --> 00:40:35,520
Wasn't it you who jammed

904
00:40:35,520 --> 00:40:36,560
our command channels?

905
00:40:36,560 --> 00:40:37,600
How could that be?

906
00:40:37,880 --> 00:40:39,840
The signal must be bad because of the rain.

907
00:40:41,600 --> 00:40:42,720
Reporting, Deputy Brigade Commander.

908
00:40:43,560 --> 00:40:44,600
This kind of weather

909
00:40:44,680 --> 00:40:46,440
is the perfect opportunity

910
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:47,600
for rigorous and strict training.

911
00:40:47,640 --> 00:40:48,560
Although the troops

912
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:49,800
suffered a setback,

913
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:51,320
they also gained experience.

914
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:53,760
Is this your idea of rigorous

915
00:40:54,400 --> 00:40:55,400
and strict?

916
00:40:56,320 --> 00:40:58,160
You're just messing around!

917
00:40:59,080 --> 00:41:00,080
How was the plan made?

918
00:41:00,640 --> 00:41:02,120
With such heavy rain,

919
00:41:02,880 --> 00:41:04,360
why didn't you adjust it in time?

920
00:41:05,200 --> 00:41:05,960
Don't explain just yet.

921
00:41:05,960 --> 00:41:06,480
Come here.

922
00:41:06,480 --> 00:41:07,120
Look for yourselves.

923
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:08,640
Our equipment...

924
00:41:08,960 --> 00:41:10,960
What has become of our precious gear?

925
00:41:11,960 --> 00:41:13,480
They've turned into lumps of mud!

926
00:41:14,960 --> 00:41:16,200
What is the point of such training?

927
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:16,960
Deputy Brigade Commander,

928
00:41:17,240 --> 00:41:18,720
this was exactly our original intention.

929
00:41:19,360 --> 00:41:20,240
Through this mobilization,

930
00:41:20,360 --> 00:41:21,920
we expose problems and solve them.

931
00:41:22,120 --> 00:41:23,640
Have you considered the cost and risks?

932
00:41:23,800 --> 00:41:24,760
Have you?

933
00:41:26,640 --> 00:41:27,520
Training

934
00:41:28,280 --> 00:41:29,600
must be solid and thorough,

935
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:31,280
taking it one step at a time.

936
00:41:32,280 --> 00:41:33,680
What's the point of taking such huge leaps?

937
00:41:33,840 --> 00:41:35,000
Not only did it violate

938
00:41:35,320 --> 00:41:36,480
the principles of our training,

939
00:41:36,520 --> 00:41:37,800
but it also carried enormous risks.

940
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:38,560
Just now,

941
00:41:38,720 --> 00:41:40,200
five armored vehicles...

942
00:41:40,400 --> 00:41:41,040
Was it five?

943
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:41,480
Yes.

944
00:41:41,560 --> 00:41:43,600
They nearly had a pile-up!

945
00:41:43,880 --> 00:41:44,960
But they didn't crash, did they?

946
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:46,120
It'd be too late if they did!

947
00:41:47,760 --> 00:41:48,760
A major accident!

948
00:41:49,680 --> 00:41:50,440
Who would take responsibility?

949
00:41:50,680 --> 00:41:51,480
I would.

950
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:52,600
Reporting to Deputy Brigade Commander Suo.

951
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:54,280
I drafted the action plan this time.

952
00:41:54,480 --> 00:41:56,000
All the problems and responsibilities fall on me.

953
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:56,800
Comrade Liang Hong,

954
00:41:57,960 --> 00:41:59,040
I am the commander.

955
00:41:59,520 --> 00:42:01,200
I take responsibility for whatever happens.

956
00:42:01,320 --> 00:42:02,280
It's not your place!

957
00:42:02,560 --> 00:42:03,360
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo,

958
00:42:03,360 --> 00:42:04,640
I am the Political Instructor.

959
00:42:04,760 --> 00:42:06,200
I cannot shirk the blame.

960
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:06,680
Enough!

961
00:42:10,400 --> 00:42:11,440
This is an exercise,

962
00:42:11,840 --> 00:42:13,000
not a play!

963
00:42:13,840 --> 00:42:15,040
And you're fighting over responsibility?

964
00:42:15,040 --> 00:42:16,200
Can you even take responsibility?

965
00:42:17,520 --> 00:42:18,320
I now order you

966
00:42:19,160 --> 00:42:21,320
to cancel all tactical scenarios during maneuvers.

967
00:42:22,760 --> 00:42:23,640
Rest and regroup on the spot.

968
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:24,880
Deputy Brigade Commander!

969
00:42:25,720 --> 00:42:27,600
The troops are in a combat state.

970
00:42:27,600 --> 00:42:28,920
How can you just pull them out like this?

971
00:42:28,920 --> 00:42:30,040
When I say pull out, we pull out.

972
00:42:30,040 --> 00:42:30,480
Deputy Brigade Commander Suo!

973
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:31,040
Stay where you are and speak.

974
00:42:31,960 --> 00:42:32,880
I assure you,

975
00:42:33,200 --> 00:42:34,040
once we cross the river,

976
00:42:34,200 --> 00:42:36,160
I will catch up with the troops immediately.

977
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:37,760
No bargaining!

978
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:38,880
Rest and regroup on the spot

979
00:42:39,080 --> 00:42:39,800
for thirty minutes.

980
00:42:41,720 --> 00:42:42,880
Find a suitable route

981
00:42:43,560 --> 00:42:44,440
and maneuver toward

982
00:42:45,240 --> 00:42:45,720
the training camp.

983
00:42:49,160 --> 00:42:50,000
Do you hear me?

984
00:42:50,880 --> 00:42:51,440
Yes, sir.
